# Neria Coaching System — Baselines, KPIs, Guardrails, and /dashboard Roadmap

## Purpose
- Establish a deterministic analytics core that defines success and learning baselines per upload.
- Constrain LLMs to interpret, coach, and propose next experiments based on provided numbers only.
- Prioritize /dashboard features that deliver ongoing, compounding value to creators.

## North Star and Stages
- North star: sustainable watch-time growth (views × average view duration).
- Stages:
  - Spark: maximize CTR and first-30s retention for new/small channels.
  - Lift: stabilize discovery via watch time per impression (WTPI) and 24h velocity.
  - Scale: compound retention, returning viewers, subs per view.

## Comparable Baselines (creator-specific)
- Compare new uploads only to the creator’s last N “similar” videos:
  - Format: Long vs Shorts vs Live.
  - Topic cluster: embeddings of title/description.
  - Length band: e.g., 6–9 min, 9–13 min.
  - Traffic source mix: Search-leaning vs Suggested/Home.
- Robust stats: rolling median and IQR (25th–75th).
- Success thresholds:
  - Win: beats `median + 0.5*IQR` in ≥2 of 3 target KPIs (CTR_24h, AVD_24h, VPH_24h).
  - Learning win: if a single lever was targeted, require improvement on that lever only.
  - Neutral/Loss: below `median - 0.5*IQR` on target KPI.

## KPI Definitions (normalize for time)
- CTR_t: click-through rate at window t.
- AVD_t: average view duration at window t.
- VPH_t: views per hour since publish at window t.
- WTPI_t: watch time per impression at window t.
- SVR_t: subs gained per 1k views at window t.
- Windows: T+1h (early), T+24h (verdict), T+7d (stickiness).

## Experiment Levers + Decisioning
- CTR lever: packaging (title/thumbnail/promise). Pass criteria: CTR_24h up, no AVD penalty.
- Retention lever: hook/pacing/structure. Pass: AVD_24h up, first-30s drop improves.
- Topic lever: audience fit/intent. Pass: WTPI_24h up, impressions growth without CTR collapse.
- Format lever: length band, Shorts cadence. Pass varies by format.

## Evaluation Windows
- T+1h: VPH_1h vs comparable baseline, early CTR rescue if < P25.
- T+24h: verdict on target lever (CTR/AVD/WTPI), traffic source mix sanity.
- T+7d: watch-time total, returning viewers, subs gained; update baselines + hypothesis bank.

## Analytics vs LLM Responsibilities
- Analytics: compute metrics, baselines, verdicts, confidence, and trends deterministically.
- LLMs ([src/utils/neria-openai.ts](mdc:src/utils/neria-openai.ts), [src/utils/neria-gemini.ts](mdc:src/utils/neria-gemini.ts)):
  - Translate numbers into one focused recommendation and “next experiment.”
  - Generate packaging alternates and script outline fixes grounded in provided metrics.
  - Guardrail: never invent metrics; only reason over supplied data.

## Competitor Intelligence (cold-start priors)
- Allowed (public): cadence, publish times, format mix, durations, titles, thumbnails, view counts, relative performance within their last N (normalize by days since publish).
- Not allowed (private): CTR, impressions, retention curves.
- Benchmarks: per-topic “hit rate,” relative velocity, packaging patterns (title length, numbers, faces/contrast/text count).
- Use for priors when creator sample size is small; replace with creator baselines as data grows.

